    "result_text": "Done. Both acceptance tests pass and the full suite is green.\n\n## What I implemented\n\n`locality` is derived from an owner's city via the fixed table (Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD), returning the canonical region or `\"UNKNOWN\"` otherwise, and exposed as a read-only field on the owner response.\n\nThree changes:\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `locality` string property to the `Owner` schema (so the generated `OwnerDto` has the field).\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/LocalityLookup.java`** (new) \u2014 a plain utility class holding the city\u2192region table and `regionFor(String)`.\n3. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 a `@Mapping(target = \"locality\", expression = \"java(LocalityLookup.regionFor(owner.getCity()))\")` on `toOwnerDto`.\n\n## The one real subtlety\n\nMy first attempt put the `regionFor`/`localityOf` helper directly on the `OwnerMapper` interface. MapStruct treats any `String \u2192 String` method on a `@Mapper` as a candidate property converter and silently applied it to **every** string field in `toOwner` \u2014 so `firstName`, `city`, `telephone`, etc. all got replaced by their \"region\" (\"UNKNOWN\", \"NSW\"\u2026), which broke owner creation with a telephone constraint violation at persist time.\n\nThe fix was to keep the helper in a **separate plain class** that's only reachable from the explicit mapping expression, so MapStruct never scans it as a conversion. (This was obscured for a while by incremental builds reusing a stale generated `OwnerMapperImpl`; a `mvn clean` is needed after mapper/openapi changes.) I verified the regenerated `toOwner` maps fields straight through and `toOwnerDto` sets `locality` via `LocalityLookup.regionFor(owner.getCity())`. I also confirmed the create pipeline itself was never at fault and left all its files untouched.\n\nVerified: `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
